  "minimalSafeRemediation": [
    "Redact observed telemetry identifier names cna,ckx,asid recursively from public URLs/object fields, including amp-encoded and percent-encoded nested URLs. Preserve exact SKU/item/quantity fields.",
    "Exclude known mmstat tracking-response cache rows independently of body size. Their shared GIF has no product evidence. Do not exclude legitimate nonempty product images or source bodies.",
    "Route public-text URL sanitation through the public sanitizer as well as embedded-token redaction.",
    "Regenerate all affected public JSON/.lino/binary projections, blobs/manifest/source rewrite mappings from retained private originals, then verify zero new requests and byte/source integrity.",
    "Add offline controls for nonempty telemetry pixels, nested/HTML-encoded identifiers, cache-ID collapse/deduplication, and unchanged genuine product facts/SKU URLs.",
    "Preserve private originals and original SHA provenance. Historical commits retain previously published pseudonymous identifiers; this review does not authorize destructive Git history rewriting."
